From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:05:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msync: Map shm pages from a zero hint, and fail cleanly when
 a mapping fails.

The server's get_shm() mapped each new shm page with
mach_vm_map(VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE) from an uninitialized
mach_vm_address_t. With ANYWHERE the kernel starts its search at the
address passed in, so stack garbage above the map's top fails with
KERN_NO_SPACE (3). The check only printed, and the memset() then wrote
through the garbage address, killing the wineserver. Every client thread
that called the server next died with it, and threads asleep in Wine
slept on: a benchmark creating 1,500 threads after a D3D12 device hung
in 7 of 42 runs on msync, each run printing
"msync: error: mach_vm_map failed with 3: (os/kern) no space available"
then "wineserver crashed", and in none with msync off.

- server: start the search at 0, and on a failure call fatal_error()
  naming the page and the error instead of touching the address.
- ntdll: when the shm map request fails, return without releasing
  receive_message's port: that static per-thread buffer still holds the
  previous reply's entry, already released.
- ntdll: refuse a reply without an entry. send_shm_to_client() sends
  MACH_PORT_NULL when mach_make_memory_entry_64() fails, and mapping
  MACH_PORT_NULL gives private zeroed memory the server never sees.
- ntdll: get_shm_slow() ends the process (abort_process(), from any
  thread) when a page can't be mapped: every caller dereferences the
  result, which was NULL plus the offset.

Local to MacNeutron; not proposed upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 server/msync.c          |  9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
index e9794a81..d8425746 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
@@ -539,6 +539,14 @@ static void *request_shm_from_server( int entry, int tid )
     if (mr != MACH_MSG_SUCCESS)
     {
         ERR( "Failed to send/receive shm map request: %#x\n", mr );
+        mach_port_deallocate( mach_task_self(), reply_port );
+        return NULL;  /* receive_message holds no new entry: don't map or release it */
+    }
+
+    if (receive_message.descriptor.name == MACH_PORT_NULL)
+    {
+        /* the server couldn't make the entry; mapping MACH_PORT_NULL would give private zeroed memory */
+        ERR( "Server sent no shm entry for %d\n", entry );
     }
     else
     {
@@ -582,7 +590,11 @@ static void *get_shm_slow( unsigned int idx )
     {
         void *addr = request_shm_from_server( entry, 0 );
         if (!addr)
+        {
+            /* every caller dereferences the result */
             ERR("Failed to map page %d (offset %#lx).\n", entry, entry * pagesize);
+            abort_process( 1 );
+        }
 
         TRACE("Mapping page %d at %p.\n", entry, addr);
 
diff --git a/server/msync.c b/server/msync.c
index 42d7c5b0..bf5ce7e4 100644
--- a/server/msync.c
+++ b/server/msync.c
@@ -712,11 +712,14 @@ static void *get_shm( unsigned int idx )
     if (!shm_addrs[entry])
     {
         kern_return_t kr;
-        mach_vm_address_t address;
+        /* VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE searches from the address passed in */
+        mach_vm_address_t address = 0;
 
-        kr = mach_vm_map( mach_task_self(), (mach_vm_address_t *)&address, (mach_vm_size_t)pagesize, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+        kr = mach_vm_map( mach_task_self(), &address, (mach_vm_size_t)pagesize, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
                           MACH_PORT_NULL, 0, FALSE, VM_PROT_DEFAULT, VM_PROT_DEFAULT, VM_INHERIT_SHARE );
-        MACH_CHECK_ERROR( kr, "mach_vm_map" );
+        if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS)
+            fatal_error( "msync: could not map shm page %d: mach_vm_map failed with %d: %s\n",
+                         entry, kr, mach_error_string( kr ) );
         memset( (void *)address, 0, pagesize );
 
         if (debug_level)
-- 
